  "articleBody": "So, you've got a new lever handle and you're ready to install it, but something isn't quite right? Don't sweat it, this happens! One of the first things to check is whether your new lever handle fits the existing bore and the latch/strike spacing. This is a common hang-up. Also, make sure it's compatible with your door's thickness – sometimes they just don't quite match up. And here's a subtle one: is your lockset for a left- or right-handed door? Getting that wrong will definitely cause problems. Start by confirming the existing hole size and spacing, then remove the old hardware. When you install the new latch and lever, pay close attention to the orientation. After everything's in, test it! Make sure the latch throws smoothly and the lever operates without any binding. If things are still off, a pro can quickly spot issues like a warped door, non-standard bore size, or a strike plate that needs a rework. We've got the tools and experience to get it sorted out for you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}